y ltx_tocentry_abstract\"><a href=\"#abstract1\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\">Abstract</span></a></li>\n184\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\"><a href=\"#S1\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">1 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Introduction</span></span></a></li>\n185\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\">\n186\t<a href=\"#S2\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">2 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">SSL-based ASD</span></span></a>\n187\t<ol class=\"ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section\">\n188\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S2.SS1\" title=\"In 2 SSL-based ASD ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">2.1 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">SSL models</span></span></a></li>\n189\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S2.SS2\" title=\"In 2 SSL-based ASD ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">2.2 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Discriminative fine-tuning</span></span></a></li>\n190\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S2.SS3\" title=\"In 2 SSL-based ASD ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">2.3 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Backend techniques</span></span></a></li>\n191\t</ol>\n192\t</li>\n193\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\">\n194\t<a href=\"#S3\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">3 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Proposed method</span></span></a>\n195\t<ol class=\"ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section\">\n196\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S3.SS1\" title=\"In 3 Proposed method ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">3.1 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Noise-aware self-supervised learning (NA-SSL)</span></span></a></li>\n197\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S3.SS2\" title=\"In 3 Proposed method ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">3.2 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Simulation of two-channel recordings</span></span></a></li>\n198\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S3.SS3\" title=\"In 3 Proposed method ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">3.3 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">ASD procedure using NA-SSL models</span></span></a></li>\n199\t</ol>\n200\t</li>\n201\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\">\n202\t<a href=\"#S4\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">4 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Experimental evaluation</span></span></a>\n203\t<ol class=\"ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section\">\n204\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S4.SS1\" title=\"In 4 Experimental evaluation ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">4.1 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Setup</span></span></a></li>\n205\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S4.SS2\" title=\"In 4 Experimental evaluation ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">4.2 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Results</span></span></a></li>\n206\t</ol>\n207\t</li>\n208\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\"><a href=\"#S5\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5 </span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Conclusion</span></span></a></li>\n209\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_bibliography\"><a href=\"#bib\" title=\"In Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\">REFERENCES</span></a></li>\n210\t</ol></nav>\n211\t</nav>\n212\t<div class=\"ltx_page_main\">\n213\t<div id=\"infobox\" class=\"infobox\">\n214\t  <a id=\"license-tr\" href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/license/index.html#licenses-available\">\n215\t    License: arXiv.org perpetual non-exclusive license\n216\t  </a>\n217\t  <div id=\"watermark-tr\">\n218\tarXiv:2608.00447v1 [eess.AS] 01 Aug 2026</div>\n219\t</div><div class=\"ltx_page_content\">\n220\t<article class=\"ltx_document ltx_authors_1line\">\n221\t<div id=\"p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n222\t<span id=\"p1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\NoHyper</span>\n223\t</div>\n224\t<h1 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_document\">Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning</h1>\n225\t\n226\t<div id=\"abstract1\" class=\"ltx_abstract\">\n227\t<h6 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_abstract\">Abstract</h6>\n228\t<p class=\"ltx_p\">In this paper, we introduce noise-aware self-supervised learning (NA-SSL) models for noise-aware anomalous sound detection (NA-ASD).\n229\tNA-ASD is an ASD task with two-channel audio recordings, where one microphone is located close to the target machine and the other is located farther away to capture noise.\n230\tFor this task, we simulate two-channel recordings using diverse audio datasets and train NA-SSL models to extract clean SSL representations of the close-microphone signal by using the far-microphone recording dominated by background noise as auxiliary information.\n231\tThe NA-SSL models are then used as frontends in the standard ASD framework.\n232\tOur experimental evaluation on the DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 development dataset demonstrates the effectiveness of the NA-SSL framework across three base SSL models (BEATs, EAT, and Dasheng), both with and without discriminative fine-tuning.\n233\tFurthermore, the challenge results proved the effectiveness of the proposed approach, where the NA-BEATs system won the challenge by a large margin, achieving an official score of 70.24%, while the second-place system achieved 65.46%.</p>\n234\t</div>\n235\t<section id=\"S1\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n236\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n237\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">1 </span><span id=\"S1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Introduction</span>\n238\t</h2>\n239\t\n240\t<div id=\"S1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n241\t<span id=\"S1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\Ac</span>\n242\t<p id=\"S1.p1.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">asd aims to detect mechanical failures from machine sounds <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib3\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">3</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib4\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">4</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib5\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">5</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib6\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">6</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib8\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">8</a>]</cite>.\n243\tSince it is infeasible to exhaustively collect rare and diverse anomalous sounds, <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> systems are developed using only normal sounds.\n244\tOne major challenge in <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> is the presence of severe background noise in factory environments during both training data collection and testing.\n245\tMotivated by this challenge,  <span title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_long\">noise-aware <abbr title=\"\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"></abbr></span></span> (<abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-ASD</span></abbr>) considers the use of auxiliary noise information <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>.\n246\t<span id=\"S1.p1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\Ac</span>naasd employs a practical two-microphone recording setup, where one microphone is placed close to the target machine and the other is placed farther away.\n247\tAlthough the far-microphone signal can also contain the target machine sound, the target sound is less dominant than in the close-microphone signal, making the far-microphone signal a useful auxiliary source of noise information.\n248\tThe <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-ASD</span></abbr> task was newly introduced in DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>, and there is strong interest in developing <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> systems that can effectively utilize such auxiliary noise information.</p>\n249\t</div>\n250\t<div id=\"S1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n251\t<p id=\"S1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">A recent trend in standard <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> tasks is the use of audio <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> models <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib9\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">9</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib10\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">10</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib11\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">11</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib12\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">12</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib13\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">13</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib8\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">8</a>]</cite>. <span id=\"S1.p2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\Ac</span>ssl models effectively capture subtle differences between normal and anomalous sounds, enabling training-free <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> by simply computing distances between a test sample and normal training samples in the representation space <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib9\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">9</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib10\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">10</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib11\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">11</a>]</cite>.\n252\t<span id=\"S1.p2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\Ac</span>ssl models fine-tuned on machine sound datasets through classification tasks using machine-information labels capture more machine-specific information and achieve <span title=\"state-of-the-art\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_long\">state-of-the-art</span></span> performance <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib12\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">12</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib13\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">13</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib8\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">8</a>]</cite>.\n253\tHowever, under noisy conditions, such representations essentially encode irrelevant background noise as well, making it difficult to focus on target machine sounds.\n254\tOne possible solution is denoising training specialized for extracting specific target machine sounds, as in WavLM <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib14\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">14</a>]</cite>.\n255\tHowever, it is not applicable to <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> tasks because clean target machine sounds are unavailable as training data.</p>\n256\t</div>\n257\t<div id=\"S1.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n258\t<p id=\"S1.p3.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">A promising approach to handling noisy conditions in audio <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> models is the  <span title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_long\">noise-aware <abbr title=\"\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"></abbr></span></span> (<abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr>) framework <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib15\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">15</a>]</cite>.\n259\t<span id=\"S1.p3.1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\Ac</span>nassl models are pre-trained on diverse audio signals to extract clean representations from noisy signals using auxiliary noise inputs.\n260\tBecause <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> models perform conditional denoising based on the provided auxiliary noise information, they do not necessarily require clean target sounds or noise samples specific to the downstream task as pre-training data.\n261\tIn <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib15\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">15</a>]</cite>, one specific implementation of the <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> framework was investigated, in which NA-BEATs was built on BEATs <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib16\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">16</a>]</cite> and noise-only segments extracted from noisy input signals were used as auxiliary noise inputs.\n262\tMore generally, the framework is expected to accommodate any auxiliary signal that captures noise information, such as the far-microphone signal available in the <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-ASD</span></abbr> task.</p>\n263\t</div>\n264\t<figure id=\"S1.F1\" class=\"ltx_figure\"><span class=\"ltx_inline-block\"><svg id=\"S1.F1.pic1\" class=\"ltx_picture ltx_centering\" height=\"177.84\" overflow=\"visible\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 362.5 177.84\" width=\"362.5\"><g transform=\"translate(0,177.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(191.95,0) translate(0,126.51)\"><g style=\"--ltx-stroke-color:#FF7300;--ltx-fill-color:#ECECEC;\" stroke=\"#FF7300\" fill=\"#ECECEC\" stroke-width=\"1.0pt\"><path d=\"M 6.23 9.69 L -184.34 9.69 C -188.16 9.69 -191.26 6.59 -191.26 2.77 L -191.26 -92.17 C -191.26 -95.99 -188.16 -99.09 -184.34 -99.09 L 6.23 -99.09 C 10.05 -99.09 13.15 -95.99 13.15 -92.17 L 13.15 2.77 C 13.15 6.59 1