\"ltx_text\"></span> <span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.3.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1354\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.3.2.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle\">\n1355\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.3.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1356\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.3.2.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\">-</span></span>\n1357\t</span></span><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.3.3\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span></td>\n1358\t<td id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb\">\n1359\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span> <span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1360\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle\">\n1361\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1362\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.2.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\">-</span></span>\n1363\t</span></span><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.4.3\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span></td>\n1364\t<td id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb\">\n1365\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.1\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span> <span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1366\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle\">\n1367\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1368\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\" style=\"padding-bottom:-2.8pt;\">61.93</span></span>\n1369\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1370\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\"><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.2.1.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(2.13)</span></span></span>\n1371\t</span></span><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.5.3\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span></td>\n1372\t<td id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb\">\n1373\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.1\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span> <span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1374\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle\">\n1375\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1376\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\" style=\"padding-bottom:-2.8pt;\"><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">62.63</span></span></span>\n1377\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1378\t<span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center\"><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.2.1.2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(1.89)</span></span></span>\n1379\t</span></span><span id=\"S4.T2.3.1.13.6.3\" class=\"ltx_text\"></span></td>\n1380\t</tr>\n1381\t</table>\n1382\t</span></div>\n1383\t</figure>\n1384\t</section>\n1385\t<section id=\"S4.SS2\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n1386\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n1387\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">4.2 </span><span id=\"S4.SS2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Results</span>\n1388\t</h3>\n1389\t\n1390\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n1391\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><a href=\"#S3.T1\" title=\"In 3.3 ASD procedure using NA-SSL models ‣ 3 Proposed method ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Table</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a> compares frontends using the same backend consisting of BEAM and <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr> with <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\gamma=4\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma=4</annotation></semantics></math>.\n1392\tFirst, we can see that <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> is effective regardless of the base model and whether discriminative fine-tuning is applied.\n1393\t<abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> yields substantial improvements of over 20% for valveEmu and also improves performance for the other machine types.\n1394\tDiscriminative fine-tuning further improves performance and achieves the best performance for all base models.\n1395\tAlso, by using pseudo labels, the benefits of discriminative fine-tuning can be observed even for machine types without attribute labels.\n1396\tWe also observe high variance in <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> performance for <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> models, highlighting the importance of ensembling multiple trials.</p>\n1397\t</div>\n1398\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n1399\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><a href=\"#S4.T2\" title=\"In 4.1 Setup ‣ 4 Experimental evaluation ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Table</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">2</span></a> shows the results obtained using different backend techniques.\n1400\tThe results demonstrate the effectiveness of the individual backend techniques and show that their benefits also carry over to <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr>-based frontends.\n1401\tIn particular, we can see that BEAM substantially improves performance.\n1402\tFor <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr>, larger values of <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\gamma\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> yield greater improvements for BEATs and Dasheng, whereas <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr> provides little benefit for EAT. These trends observed for <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr> are consistent with the findings reported in <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib11\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">11</a>]</cite>.</p>\n1403\t</div>\n1404\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n1405\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p3.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We also conducted an ablation study to evaluate the effect of applying <abbr title=\"low-rank adaptation\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">LoRA</span></abbr> to the NA layers during discriminative fine-tuning, as shown in <a href=\"#S4.T3\" title=\"In 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Experimental evaluation ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Table</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">3</span></a>.\n1406\tAlthough discriminative fine-tuning remains effective even without <abbr title=\"low-rank adaptation\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">LoRA</span></abbr> in the NA layers, applying <abbr title=\"low-rank adaptation\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">LoRA</span></abbr> to the NA layers tends to yield better performance.</p>\n1407\t</div>\n1408\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p4\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n1409\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p4.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><a href=\"#S4.F3\" title=\"In 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Experimental evaluation ‣ Anomalous Sound Detection Meets Noise-Aware Self-Supervised Learning\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Figure</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">3</span></a> shows the results on the DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 evaluation dataset reported in <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib33\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">33</a>]</cite>.\n1410\tIt compares our Dis NA-BEATs with the ten top-performing systems <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib34\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">34</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib35\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">35</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib36\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">36</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib37\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">37</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib38\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">38</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib39\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">39</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib40\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">40</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib41\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">41</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib42\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">42</a>]</cite> and the official baseline system <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>. Here, the backend consists of BEAM and <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr> with <math id=\"S4.SS2.p4.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\gamma=4\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma=4</annotation></semantics></math>, and the anomaly scores from three trials are ensembled.\n1411\tDis NA-BEATs ranked first on the evaluation dataset with an official score of 70.24%, surpassing the second-place system (65.46%) and the official baseline system (59.80%) by a considerable margin.\n1412\tIt is also noteworthy that our Dis NA-BEATs is built on only a single base <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> model with a single backend, whereas the other systems rely on ensembles of multiple <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> models <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib35\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">35</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib40\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">40</a>]</cite> and multiple backends <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib35\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">35</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib38\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">38</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib39\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">39</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib40\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">40</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib42\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">42</a>]</cite>.\n1413\tMoreover, our Dis NA-BEATs outperforms the other BEATs-based systems <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib35\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">35</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib39\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">39</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib40\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">40</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib42\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">42</a>]</cite>.</p>\n1414\t</div>\n1415\t<figure id=\"S4.T3\" class=\"ltx_table\">\n1416\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_table\">Table 3: </span>Ablation study of discriminative fine-tuning.\n1417\tThe values are harmonic mean of the official scores over machine types in the development dataset.\n1418\tThe values are reported as “Mean (CI95)”.\n1419\tThe backend consists of BEAM and <abbr title=\"relative deviation pooling\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">RDP</span></abbr> with <math id=\"S4.T3.2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\gamma=4\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma=4</annotation></semantics></math>.\n1420\tNA denotes <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> pre-training, and Dis denotes discriminative fine-tuning.\n1421\t</figcaption>\n1422\t<div id=\"S4.T3.3\" class=\"ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer\" style=\"width:433.6pt;height:61.7pt;vertical-align:-27.7pt;\"><span class=\"ltx_transformed_inner\" style=\"transform:translate(44.1pt,-6.3pt) scale(1.25505047081197,1.25505047081197) ;\">\n1423\t<table id=\"S4.T3.3.1\" class=\"ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle\">\n1424\t<tr id=\"S4.T3.3.1.1\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1425\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt\">Method</td>\n1426\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.1.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt\">BEATs</td>\n1427\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.1.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt\">EAT</td>\n1428\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.1.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt\">Dasheng</td>\n1429\t</tr>\n1430\t<tr id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1431\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t\">NA</td>\n1432\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t\">63.64 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(1.71)</span>\n1433\t</td>\n1434\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t\">62.74 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(1.41)</span>\n1435\t</td>\n1436\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t\">61.33 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.2.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(2.13)</span>\n1437\t</td>\n1438\t</tr>\n1439\t<tr id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1440\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left\">Dis NA</td>\n1441\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right\">\n1442\t<span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">64.32</span> <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.2.2\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(0.77)</span>\n1443\t</td>\n1444\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right\">\n1445\t<span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">63.88</span> <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.3.2\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(0.30)</span>\n1446\t</td>\n1447\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right\">61.93 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.3.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(2.13)</span>\n1448\t</td>\n1449\t</tr>\n1450\t<tr id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4\" class=\"ltx_tr\">\n1451\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.1\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb\">Dis NA w/o LoRA in NA layers</td>\n1452\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.2\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb\">63.97 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(1.81)</span>\n1453\t</td>\n1454\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.3\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb\">63.17 <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(1.17)</span>\n1455\t</td>\n1456\t<td id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.4\" class=\"ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb\">\n1457\t<span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">62.09</span> <span id=\"S4.T3.3.1.4.4.2\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:70%;\">(0.84)</span>\n1458\t</td>\n1459\t</tr>\n1460\t</table>\n1461\t</span></div>\n1462\t</figure>\n1463\t<figure id=\"S4.F3\" class=\"ltx_figure\">\n1464\t<p id=\"S4.F3.1\" class=\"ltx_p ltx_align_center\"><span id=\"S4.F3.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1465\t<span id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer\" style=\"width:276.1pt;height:80.6pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;\"><span class=\"ltx_transformed_inner\" style=\"transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;\">\n1466\t<span id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">\n1467\t\n1468\t\n1469\t <span class=\"ltx_inline-block\"><svg id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1.1.1.pic1\" class=\"ltx_picture\" height=\"111.47\" overflow=\"visible\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 354.33 111.47\" width=\"354.33\"><g style=\"--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;\" transf