"><span class=\"ltx_foreignobject_content\"><span id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1.1.1.pic1.54.54.54.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:80%;\">70</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style=\"--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;\" transform=\"matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -36.07 10.45)\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\"><foreignObject style=\"--ltx-fo-width:5.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;\" width=\"72.63\" height=\"8.65\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)\" overflow=\"visible\"><span class=\"ltx_foreignobject_container\"><span class=\"ltx_foreignobject_content\"><span id=\"S4.F3.1.1.1.1.1.pic1.55.55.55.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\" style=\"font-size:90%;\">Official score</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></span></span>\n1470\t</span></span></span></p>\n1471\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure\">Figure 3: </span>\n1472\tComparison of our Dis NA-BEATs with the ten top-performing systems and the official baseline system on the DCASE 2026 Challenge Task 2 evaluation dataset.\n1473\t</figcaption>\n1474\t</figure>\n1475\t</section>\n1476\t</section>\n1477\t<section id=\"S5\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n1478\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n1479\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">5 </span><span id=\"S5.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Conclusion</span>\n1480\t</h2>\n1481\t\n1482\t<div id=\"S5.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n1483\t<p id=\"S5.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">In this paper, we explored the use of <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> models for the <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-ASD</span></abbr> task.\n1484\tThe <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> models aim to extract clean <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> representations from noisy signals by leveraging auxiliary noise information captured by a microphone located farther from the target sound source.\n1485\tThese models are first pre-trained on simulated two-channel recordings constructed from diverse audio signals.\n1486\tThey are then used as frontends within a well-established <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr>-based <abbr title=\"anomalous sound detection\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">ASD</span></abbr> framework.\n1487\tOur experimental results demonstrated the general effectiveness and broad compatibility of the <abbr title=\"noise-aware   ()\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">NA-SSL</span></abbr> framework across three base <abbr title=\"self-supervised learning\" class=\"ltx_glossaryref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_glossary_short\">SSL</span></abbr> models, multiple backend methods, and configurations both with and without discriminative fine-tuning.</p>\n1488\t</div>\n1489\t</section>\n1490\t<section id=\"bib\" class=\"ltx_bibliography\">\n1491\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_bibliography\">REFERENCES</h2>\n1492\t\n1493\t<ul class=\"ltx_biblist\">\n1494\t<li id=\"bib.bib1\" class=\"ltx_bibitem\">\n1495\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_bibitem\">[1]</span>\n1496\t<span class=\"ltx_bibblock\">\n1497\tY. Koizumi, Y. Kawaguchi, K. Imoto, T. Nakamura, Y. Nikaido, R. Tanabe, H. Purohit, K. Suefusa, T. Endo, M. Yasuda <em id=\"bib.bib1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">et al.</em>, “Description and discussion on DCASE2020 challenge task2: Unsupervised anomalous sound detection for machine condition monitoring,” in <em id=\"bib.bib1.2.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">Proc. DCASE</em>, 2020, pp. 81–85.\n1498\t\n1499\t</span>\n1500\t</li>\n1501